---
title: "Healing Breakfast Oatmeal"
summary: "A new take on oatmeal to help heal your digestive system and fuel you with nutrients for the day."
publishedDate: 2019-03-01
heroImage: /images/recipes/healing-breakfast-oatmeal.webp
pillar: gut-health
cta: book-consult
prepMinutes: 10
cookMinutes: 10
servings: "3 Servings"
ingredients:
  - "1 ½ cups coconut milk"
  - "5 Tbl coconut flour"
  - "2 Tbl coconut flakes"
  - "pinch salt"
  - "3 eggs"
  - "1 banana"
  - "1 tsp cinnamon"
  - "¼ cup sweet potato or pumpkin puree"
  - "¼ cup raisins – optional"
  - "3 Tbl ground flax"
  - "3 Tbl hemp seeds"
steps:
  - "In a small pot, whisk together the coconut milk, flour, flakes and salt."
  - "Heat over medium-low heat just until begins to bubble and boil. Remove from heat, allow to cool for a few minutes."
  - "While that cools, mash the banana in a small bowl, add eggs, sweet potato/pumpkin, and whisk to combine."
  - "Slowly add the egg-banana mixture to the warm coconut milk, whisking as you do so."
  - "Return to medium-low heat (not too hot!), and whisk slowly. Add cinnamon, and raisins if using."
  - "Allow mixture to thicken for about 4-5 minutes, continuing to stir."
  - "Remove from heat, add flax and hemp seeds, stir to combine."
  - "Serve with milk of choice and fresh berries."
  - "Store in airtight container in fridge for up to 5 days."
legacyUrl: /breakfast/healing-breakfast-oatmeal
---

A gluten-and-grain-free version of oatmeal that is easy on the digestive system yet full of fiber and protein.
